        "5. **Multiple Regression: StressSurvey + Time.** Run a multiple regression of Anxiety on both **StressSurvey** and Time. What are the estimated coefficients? How do they compare to the true coefficients?\n",
        "\n",
        "The coefficients are as seen below. The coefficients for Stress Survey are off by 43%, while the intercept is off by .589 units. These aren't too wildly off, but the time coefficient is, -2800% off in fact. This is likely because of issues in running regressions when two variables are correlated with one another. The coefficients lose their interpretability and reliability. "
      ],
      "id": "3eb54864"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: multiple-regression-stresssurvey-time\n",
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import r2_score\n",
        "\n",
        "y = observDF['Anxiety'].values\n",
        "X = np.column_stack([\n",
        "    observDF['StressSurvey'].values,\n",
        "    observDF['Time'].values,\n",
        "])\n",
        "model_stresssurvey_time = LinearRegression()\n",
        "model_stresssurvey_time.fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Coefficient (StressSurvey): {model_stresssurvey_time.coef_[0]:.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Coefficient (Time): {model_stresssurvey_time.coef_[1]:.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Intercept: {model_stresssurvey_time.intercept_:.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"R-squared: {r2_score(y, model_stresssurvey_time.predict(X)):.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "multiple-regression-stresssurvey-time",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
